## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical DR design: cross-region replication, active-active components, idempotent processing, and observable validation under real outage scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- DR and RTO/RPO
- Pub/Sub exactly-once delivery
- Cloud Run warm-standby
- Spanner multi-region vs Cloud SQL replication
- Dataflow streaming to BigQuery
- Per-environment isolation
- Observability and chaos testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js Pub/Sub subscriber skeleton with idempotent dedup logic
const {PubSub} = require('@google-cloud/pubsub');
const dedupe = new Set();
exports.receiveEvent = async (msg, context) => {
  const id = msg.attributes?.messageId || msg.id;
  if (dedupe.has(id)) {
    msg.ack();
    return;
  }
  dedupe.add(id);
  // process
  msg.ack();
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify RTO/RPO in production and CI/CD?
- What metrics and alarms would you define to detect a failover failure?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests familiarity with GCP primitives for multi-tenant secrets, security isolation, API design, and basic caching/observability, suitable for a beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- Secret Manager with per-tenant secrets and IAM isolation
- Cloud Run security and API key authentication
- Lightweight cache to reduce Secret Manager calls (60s)
- Observability via Cloud Logging and Monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
const {SecretManagerServiceClient} = require('@google-cloud/secret-manager');
const client = new SecretManagerServiceClient();

async function accessSecretVersion(name) {
  const [version] = await client.accessSecretVersion({ name });
  return version.payload.data.toString('utf8');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate API keys and enforce revocation?
